-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A note on why this license, before the license itself.

This is a personal tool. It runs one person's internship search on one Raspberry
Pi, against one resume. It was published so that it could be read, not so that
it could be sold.

Read it, fork it, learn from it, run it for yourself, take the ideas into your
own work. That is all permitted and it is the reason the repository is public.
Reviewing or running it to evaluate the author for employment is noncommercial
use and is explicitly fine.

What is not permitted without asking first is shipping it, or something built on
it, as a commercial product or service. If that is what you want, open an issue.
The answer is very likely yes.

The operative terms below are the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0,
unmodified. It is used rather than something written here because a homemade
license is a liability for everyone who reads it.

Earlier commits of this repository were published under the MIT License. That
grant is not revoked and cannot be. Anyone who obtained a copy under those terms
keeps them for that copy.

